value "{\\lambda }_{2}<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306232}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71795f8c-56a0-58f5-9c16-c4903d72ee1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}<0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306232} :answer-field/id #uuid "98cb72e1-862a-5bae-8689-2c815f9ee823" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90c50232-7602-52cc-ac73-1fc9e380cce4" :question/math-academy-id "q-333041" :question/problem "![](images/56/56a90f9fb61640cc2eeca8e2f21f69381a1d53d008701ec457ade0fed7e54a64.png)\n\nThe phase portrait for a system of linear differential equations whose matrix has two real, distinct eigenvalues is shown above.\nThe eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[2,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }1]^{T},$ respectively. \nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-2}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach \n{{field-3}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-4}}.\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny={{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing \n{{field-6}},\nmeaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach \n{{field-7}} \nas $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have \n{{field-8}}." :question/worked-solution "The straight-line solutions of the system have the form\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,{c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2}x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/1f/1f166fad96cd30dbc0b9cf05fdabcccd26cd68e25fc26b91ae357d4015813614.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{away from the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach $\\text{infinity}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{1}>0.$\n\nThe line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-x,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/cb/cbb8268b959a09af3d0b57573ff08f45a2fb87f376d87f284df49cd5094412d9.png)\n\nThe tangents along this line are pointing $\\text{toward the origin},$ meaning that the solutions of the form \n${c}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nmust approach $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, we must have ${\\lambda }_{2}<0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186422156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166917 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13af6d27-628d-5bdb-b396-299d9cfd64e7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Parameters of a System Given Its Phase Portrait"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "538b6e5d-fd93-5930-ad67-61e5d1d45c29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422051} {:answer/id #uuid "8553e79f-346e-52b1-ad80-d5bffb94983f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }_{2}"